                <pb facs="0524" n="442" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg442"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/1143.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-03-30"><hi rendition="#italic">March 30,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>This embassy has received a note from the Italian minister asking what will be
                    the attitude of the Government of the United States as to the application to our
                    nationals of the suspension of constitutional guaranties by the Mexican
                    Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
